==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|indefinite|-ly<id:adverbial>}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈdɛfɪnɪtli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-indefinitely.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyph|en|in|def|i|nite|ly}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In a manner that is not [[definite]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''indefinitely''' determined fossil}}
# For a long time, with no defined end.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1905|author=Lloyd Osbourne|title=Baby Bullet: the motor of destiny|page=171|passage=It was a dark, horsehairy place with a sort of abandon-hope atmosphere that seemed suitable for people that had no money, and who were going '''indefinitely''' into pawn.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020-05-20|author=David Thrower; Ian Wray|title=Revisiting the plan for developing the North's rail network|journal=Rail|page=40|text=One argument is that "the virus has changed everything" and that people will work from home and travel much less, easing capacity pressures.<br>But there is a counter argument whereby we may all discover that, longer-term, many jobs cannot after all be effectively carried out from home '''indefinitely'''.}}
# {{U|forever}}.

